surface-arclength-reference-load.out
Material arc length keeps external reference loads fixed in equilibrium, residuals and reactions
StaticStructural solverType "matcalm" loadlevelguess 1.0 nsteps 1 deltat 1.0 stepLength 0.02 Psi 0. hpc 2 2 1 MaxIter 30 rtolv 1.e-11 rtolf 1.e-11 manrmsteps 1 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 2dPlaneStress
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all
ndofman 8 nelem 8 ncrosssect 2 nmat 2 nbc 6 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 6
# Four independent unit segments, each with two coincident membrane elements. Their combined energy is
# W(s,Lambda) = 0.5 Lambda s - 0.5 s + 0.5 (s^2 - 1) - ln(s), s = 1 + u_right.
# The first two segments have no external force on their free dof. HPC selects s=0.98, so equilibrium gives
# Lambda = 1 - 2 (s - 1/s) = 1.0808163265306122. Both have a unit force on the fixed left end: reference
# on segment 1, ordinary on segment 2. Material CALM keeps both forces fixed, hence both reactions are -1.
# Segments 3 and 4 have the same force 0.1 on the free right dof (reference and ordinary, respectively).
# At the same Lambda, s - 1/s = 0.1 + 0.5 - 0.5 Lambda. Its positive root gives u=0.030239718263849635,
# and the left reaction is -0.1. A reference load must not be multiplied by the material load level.
node 1 coords 2 0 0
node 2 coords 2 1 0
node 3 coords 2 0 0
node 4 coords 2 1 0
node 5 coords 2 0 0
node 6 coords 2 1 0
node 7 coords 2 0 0
node 8 coords 2 1 0
lineplanestrainsurface 1 nodes 2 1 2 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 2 nodes 2 1 2 crosssect 2 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 3 nodes 2 3 4 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 4 nodes 2 3 4 crosssect 2 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 5 nodes 2 5 6 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 6 nodes 2 5 6 crosssect 2 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 7 nodes 2 7 8 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 8 nodes 2 7 8 crosssect 2 nlgeo 1
simplesurfacecs 1 material 1
simplesurfacecs 2 material 2
surfacetensionmat 1 gamma1 0.5 d 1 arclenghtpar 1
surfacetensionmat 2 gamma1 -0.5 mu 1 d 1
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 0 set 2
NodalLoad 3 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 1.0 set 3 reference
NodalLoad 4 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 1.0 set 4
NodalLoad 5 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 0.1 set 5 reference
NodalLoad 6 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 0.1 set 6
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1
Set 1 nodes 4 1 3 5 7
Set 2 nodes 8 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8
Set 3 nodes 1 1
Set 4 nodes 1 3
Set 5 nodes 1 6
Set 6 nodes 1 8
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-9
